hypotheses.statement:
Let $\ell=1/(2\sqrt2)$ and define the Euclidean similarity $$\Phi(x_0,y_0,z_0)=(-\ell x_0,\ell y_0,\ell(1-z_0)).$$ Then $\Phi K_0=K_1$, and the two sets in <a href="#c:uncentered-sweeps" data-reference-type="eqref" data-reference="c:uncentered-sweeps">[c:uncentered-sweeps]</a> are carried exactly to the two sets in <a href="#c:rat-sweeps" data-reference-type="eqref" data-reference="c:rat-sweeps">[c:rat-sweeps]</a> with $$\label{c:rational-parameter-dictionary}
 d=d_0/2,\qquad \epsilon=4(1+d_0)k,
 \qquad q=\eta_0 k^2/2.$$ In particular $q=\eta\epsilon^2$ where $\eta=\eta_0/[32(1+d_0)^2]$. All perpendicular areas are multiplied by $1/8$.

